ance Internal Control Risk Management Compliance Intellectual Property Information Security Data Certifications ESG Data Policies Investor Relations Open the Investor Relations menu Latest IR Information Latest Downloads Management Information Top Message Corporate Philosophy Mid-Term Business Plan Disclosure Policy Sustainability Stock Information Basic Stock Information Major Shareholders Procedures General Meeting of Shareholders Electronic Public Notice Promoting Dialogue with Shareholders and Disclosure Business & Financial Data At a glance Financial Information IR Library Financial Results (Tanshin) Financial Results Presentation Materials Annual & Semiannual Securities Reports Timely Disclosure Information Integrated Reports News Careers Purchase Counter Home Sustainability ... Governance Information Security Information Security 1. Basic Policy We recognize ensuring information security as an important social responsibility in our business activities, and we handle all information assets obtained from business partners, employees, and other third parties appropriately, manage, and protect them safely and appropriately. Additionally, we implement appropriate measures and management according to risks such as information leakage, loss, or falsification caused by cyberattacks, and work to prevent information security incidents and promote continuous improvement. Basic Information Security Policy 2. Promotion of Initiatives Hirose Electric established the “Basic Information Security Policy” in 2008 and expanded it across the entire Hirose Group in 2017. This policy recognizes the importance of ensuring information security and advocates properly handling all information assets and ensuring safe and appropriate management and protection. Within the Hirose Group, the President and CEO and the Head of the Administration Headquarters serve as the overall information security officer, and we have established the “Information Security Measures Team” as a subordinate organization under the CSR and Risk Management Committee. We have established an information security management system across the entire group, and are working to improve information security levels through strengthening cyberattack countermeasures, information leak prevention, and awareness activities, and continuously working on improvement. Additionally, based on the annual information security risk assessment, we formulate and implement a risk response plan. Furthermore, we provide information security education and initial response drills for executives and all group employees to prevent accidents and raise awareness of information security. Additionally, the CSR and Risk Management Committee meets quarterly to report on the progress of risk response plans and the activities of the information security task force to the overall information security officer. Based on corrective actions based on improvement instructions in response, we continuously operate the PDCA cycle. Furthermore, since 2026 we have been working toward obtaining ISO 27001 certification, an international standard for information security management. Centered around the headquarters’ information security measures team, we promote group unification of information security rules, establishment of information asset management ledgers, establishment and training of response systems in the event of major incidents, and mutual audits between departments. Additionally, to respond to the increasing sophistication of recent cyberattacks, we are enhancing technical measures such as strengthening system and network defenses and enhancing monitoring systems, as well as strengthening personnel measures such as conducting regular education for employees. Sustainability Sustainability Approach and Basic Policy Environment Environmental Responsibility Climate Change Chemical Substances Effective Use of Resources Biodiversity Society Human Capital Health Management Human Rights Quality Supply Chain Governance C